Phishing Detection ML Project

This project is a **Machine Learning-based phishing detection system** that predicts whether a URL is phishing or legitimate using a structured dataset of URL features. The model is trained using a Random Forest Classifier and can be extended to other algorithms.

---

 Project Structure

PHISHING-DETECTION-ML/
│
├── data/
│ ├── raw/ # Raw datasets (original CSV files)
│ └── processed/ # Processed/cleaned datasets ready for modeling
├── models/
│ └── phishing_model.pkl # Trained ML model
├── src/
│ ├── init.py
│ ├── preprocessing.py # Data cleaning and preprocessing functions
│ ├── features.py # Feature extraction functions
│ ├── train_model.py # Model training script
│ ├── evaluate.py # Model evaluation utilities
├── README.md # Project documentation
---

 Features

- Cleans and preprocesses raw data (handles duplicates, missing values, and encodes categorical features)  
- Extracts features for ML modeling  
- Trains a **Random Forest Classifier**  
- Evaluates the model using:
  - Accuracy
  - Precision
  - Recall
  - F1-score
  - Confusion matrix  
- Saves the trained model to `models/phishing_model.pkl` for future predictions

